<td>— , queued for the Storage task (done in order; a <code>DATA_READ</code> answers <code>busy</code> until it is). Calibration or the update area: <code>refused</code>; misaligned, across a page, empty: <code>bad argument</code>; <code>STAMP</code> of another layout: <code>invalid</code> and why; <code>busy</code>: the other port writes, or the queue is full (send it again). From Bluetooth: <code>refused</code>. The first one stops the store's own records until a restart (LINK-61). <code>STAMP</code>: the header sector erased and the layout 3 header written (below), then the radio restarts, as after <code>REBOOT</code> (LINK-62)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>0x63 <code>CLOCK</code></td>
<td>optionally UTC seconds (u32, 2020-2099)</td>
<td>UTC seconds now (u32; 0 no time yet), the clock's source (u8: 0 none, 1 GPS, 2 set by hand or over the link). With seconds: the clock set as 0 6 6 sets it by hand (GPS-23; GPS time takes over at the next fix while 0 6 6 says "from GPS"); out of range or another length <code>bad argument</code>. Only from radios whose second capability byte says 4 (LINK-65)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>0x60 <code>STOCK_RESTORE</code></td>
<td>op (u8), then: 0 <code>START</code> (nothing; the cable only, not while transmitting); 1 <code>ERASE</code> sector address (u32); 2 <code>PROGRAM</code> address (u32), 1-128 bytes within one 256-byte page; 3 <code>CRC</code> address (u32), length (u32); 4 <code>FINISH</code></td>
<td><code>START</code>: chip size (u32), the calibration sector's CRC-32 (u32), range count (u8), each range's start and end (u32), then the MCU's unique ID (12 bytes, its three words little-endian, lowest first; decision 263): the radio stops and serves only these requests until it resets (other types: <code>busy</code>). <code>ERASE</code>/<code>PROGRAM</code>: <code>refused</code> outside the ranges, in calibration or the update area; <code>bad argument</code> misaligned. <code>CRC</code>: the CRC-32 (u32). <code>FINISH</code>: then the radio resets into the bootloader, saving nothing (BACKUP-7, decision 261)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Records</strong> (<code>what</code>; the same layouts the radio stores):</p>
