<p><strong>APRS records</strong> (<code>HEARD</code>, <code>MSGS</code> and their events; LINK-44). A station: flags (u8: 1 a position follows, 2 course and speed, 4 altitude), callsign (length, text), symbol (u8: 0 car, 1 home, 2 digi, 3 weather, 4 handheld, 5 iGate, 6 truck, 7 boat), age (u32, seconds), times heard (u16), then the latitude and longitude (2 × i32, degrees × 1e7), course (u16, degrees) and speed (u16, km/h), altitude (i32, m) as the flags say, the path (length, text: the digipeaters, the used one marked <code>*</code>; empty when heard direct), the comment (length, text, up to 40). A message: in (u8: 1 to us, 0 ours), state (u8: 0 unread, 1 read, 2 pending, 3 acked, 4 retrying, 5 failed, 6 rejected: APRS-34; a reader shows a value it doesn't know as unknown), tries (u8, while retrying), age (u32, seconds), who (length, text: from, or to), the text (length, text).</p>
<p><strong>Events</strong> (<code>EVENT</code>'s payload, LINK-46): kind 1 a station heard: the heard list's count (u8), the station. Kind 2 a new message, in or out: the count (u16), the message. Kind 3 a message's state changed: the count (u16), the message as it is now. Kind 4 Live View: below. Kind 5 an event logged (LINK-57): the record as <code>LOG_READ</code> gives it (below), its sequence number first; oldest first, each once.</p>
<p><strong>Live View</strong> (kind 4, LINK-47, LINK-48; shared code: <code>ferrite-core</code> <code>liveview.rs</code>, a client in <code>tools/ferrite_link.py</code>'s <code>LiveView</code>). The compact form is the <code>UI</code> readback's lines (up to 48) less <code>state</code>'s <code>frame=</code> and <code>ago=</code>, each line cut after its last whole token that fits 230 coded bytes. A line's tokens are split at the spaces outside double quotes (inside them a backslash escapes the next byte); joining them with one space gives the line. Text on the wire is coded: a byte 0x01-0x1F stands for that entry of the dictionary (version 1), any other byte for itself:</p>
