<p>(␣ is a space.) An update: seq (u8), flags (u8: 1 the whole state: drop every line first; 2 more follows soon: the check isn't valid yet), check (u16: FNV-1a 32 over every line, each followed by <code>\n</code>, its low 16 bits), lines (u8: the count after; new lines start empty), then ops to the end, each led by a byte whose top two bits are the op and the low six the line:</p>
<ul>
<li>0 LINE: length (u8), the line, coded.</li>
<li>1 TOKENS: the line's token count after (u8), entries (u8), then each entry: token index (u8; bit 7: the value only, the token's key up to its first <code>=</code> is the one there), length (u8), the token or the value, coded. Tokens past the count go; new ones start empty.</li>
<li>2 TOKENS with the count unchanged: as 1 without the count byte.</li>
</ul>
<p>A client applies an update only if it carries the whole state or the seq after the last one it applied, then, unless more follows, checks its lines against the check; otherwise (a lost or late update, a mismatch) it sends <code>SUBSCRIBE</code> without renew and gets the whole state. The radio diffs against what it last sent this session (1 KB of the lines' text, longer screens' lines by hash and then sent whole), so an update is exact. A meter moving on one card is one op of 11 bytes (op 2 on the card's line, two entries: <code>s=</code>'s value <code>"S3"</code> and <code>meter=</code>'s), 17 with the kind and header, 23 on the wire.</p>
<p><strong>Layouts and the update</strong> (LINK-59 – LINK-62, UPD-16, decision 333). What Console needs to move a radio's data from layout 2 to layout 3 with <code>DATA_READ</code> and <code>DATA_WRITE</code> alone; shared code: <code>ferrite-core</code> <code>layout.rs</code> (the map), <code>ferrite-store</code> <code>records.rs</code> (the records), <code>store.rs</code> (the header), <code>logs.rs</code> (the rings). Little-endian throughout; CRC-16 is CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE (poly 0x1021, init 0xFFFF, no reflection, no final XOR), CRC-32 is CRC-32/ISO-HDLC (as <code>DATA_READ</code>'s).</p>
