</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Then the sector of layout 3 that holds layout 2's header (0x02C000, channel sector 28) last, then <code>STAMP</code> with layout 3: the radio restarts, checks every zone's count against its channels (CHAN-36) and comes up with the settings, slots, channels and lists as they were.</p>
<hr />
<h2 id="constants-in-the-firmware">Constants in the firmware</h2>
<p>Every message type, record kind, capability bit and limit, as <code>ferrite-core/src/link.rs</code> defines them (its doc comment beside each). The text above is the spec; this table is what the firmware builds with.</p>
