<tr>
<td><code>BT_BAUD</code></td>
<td><code>9_600</code></td>
<td>Bluetooth's UART rate (LINK-25, decision 152): the BT513 module's resting rate, 9600 8N1. Stock V0.27 sends its KISS(BLE) frames to the module at 9600 (0x08016EEC: USART1 restarted at 0x2580 through 0x08023F68, the frame written, then back to 115200); stock's own 115200 is for its CPS programming (most likely the vendor's app sets the module to 115200 first: its FF31 handshake carries a rate byte).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>BT_FAST</code></td>
<td><code>115_200</code></td>
<td>Bluetooth's fast rate (LINK-25.1, decision 285): the module's UART after the per-connection speed unlock (FF31, selector 02), which a host writes once the radio has agreed to <code>BAUD</code> 115200 on Bluetooth. The module keeps it across BLE connections and loses it when powered off (bench, Oct 24, 2026: <code>docs/research/ble-speed.md</code>).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>BT_RATES</code></td>
