</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>FAST</code></td>
<td><code>BtPace { burst: 160, gap_ms: 100 }</code></td>
<td>At <code>BT_FAST</code> (LINK-36.1): 160-byte bursts, 100 ms apart (about 1.6 KB/s). The module takes bursts of about 160 bytes at 115200 but passes on only about 1.6 KB/s on average to a Mac (6-8 notifications every ~30 ms interval, some intervals missed), and still forwards only after its UART has been quiet: 160 B every 50 ms lost about 1 reply in 3, and a steady trickle of 20-byte pieces at 1.6 KB/s lost 7 of 10; 80 B / 50 ms and 160 B / 100 ms passed 10 of 10 (bench, Oct 24, 2026).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>MAX_GAP_MS</code></td>
<td><code>1_000</code></td>
