</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>OFF</code></td>
<td><code>0</code></td>
<td>Unkey: always <code>ok</code>, keyed or not, so a PC can send it whatever happened.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>ON</code></td>
<td><code>1</code></td>
<td>Key up, with every transmit check a PTT press has; then a byte: the slot (<code>ACTIVE</code>, or 0-2 for A-C). <code>ok</code> and the slot keyed, or <code>invalid</code> and the reason as text.</td>
